# Conventional Commits v1.0.0 — https://www.conventionalcommits.org/en/v1.0.0/
#
# Format:
#
#   <type>[optional scope][!]: <subject>
#
#   <body>
#
#   <footer>
#
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#   type     feat, fix, docs, style, refactor, perf, test, build, ci,
#            chore, revert
#   scope    optional — section of the codebase (e.g. api, cli, auth)
#   !        flag a BREAKING CHANGE before the colon
#   subject  imperative, lowercase, no trailing period, ≤ 72 chars
#
#   body     explain *why* the change is needed, not *what*. Wrap at 72.
#            Link issues with "Refs: #123" or "Closes: #123".
#
#   footer   one token/value pair per line:
#              BREAKING CHANGE: <description of the break and migration>
#              Refs: #123
#              Closes: #456
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Example:
#
#   feat(api): add paginated list endpoint
#
#   Previously the list endpoint returned every record at once, which timed
#   out for tenants over 10k rows. Add offset/limit query params and return
#   400 when either exceeds the configured max.
#
#   BREAKING CHANGE: clients must now pass offset and limit; omitting
#   them returns 400.
#
#   Closes: #42
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

<type>[optional scope][!]: <subject>


<Replace this line with the body. Wrap at 72 chars. Use "Refs: #123" or "Closes: #123" to link issues.>


<Replace this line with footer token/value pairs (BREAKING CHANGE:, Refs:, Closes:). Delete this section if not needed.>
